READING. The correction goes the WRONG WAY for `rep_dC`: it does not
explain any of the offset, it enlarges what has to be explained -- and by
more than re-centring the prior would relieve. So R2 should be ruled
against the LARGER residue, not the smaller one. ⚠ Gamma is the weak input
and is a BAND; an observational mass-weighted stratospheric age would
close it, and is the one download that would sharpen this.
⛔ Nothing adopted; no parameter and no prior is changed here.
